cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ImmunoMath in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "ImmunoMath: evaluation of probabilistic genetic inference"
abstract: >-
  ImmunoMath (framework name: Metrognome) is an open-source Python library for
  evaluating probabilistic genetic inference using proper scoring rules,
  calibration diagnostics, and cohort statistics. It is an evaluation library,
  not an inference library.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Society for Immune Polymorphism (SIP)"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/societyforimmunepolymorphism/immunomath"
url: "https://github.com/societyforimmunepolymorphism/immunomath"
keywords:
  - probabilistic forecasting
  - proper scoring rules
  - calibration
  - HLA
  - genotype imputation
  - evaluation
